* TR10 RX_AM_DEMOD -- transistor-level I/Q rectifier and summer for AM.
*
* The mixer + TIA already downconvert the AM carrier to baseband, so the
* TIA outputs are the audio envelope riding on a DC bias (~1.55 V).  This
* block recovers the audio:
*
*   1. Compare each channel with a stiff 1.55 V reference that matches
*      the TIA output DC bias.
*   2. Apply the channel and the reference to an NMOS differential pair.
*   3. A PMOS mirror subtracts the reference-branch current, leaving a net
*      current that is positive only when the channel is above its bias.
*      A diode-connected NMOS clamps the negative half and an NMOS mirror
*      copies the rectified current to the shared output node.
*   4. The I and Q rectified currents sum into Rload/Cload.  With the LO
*      phase-locked to the carrier the Q channel is near zero, so the sum
*      is the I audio.  Without a PLL the sum is |I|+|Q|, which tracks the
*      envelope to within 3 dB over all LO phases.
*
* Ports: i_in q_in out vdd vss
*   i_in/q_in  TIA outputs, DC ~1.55 V, audio on top
*   out        audio, DC ~5 V - Irect*Rload, AC coupled by the next stage
*
* Default: itail=1 mA, rload=10k, cload=3.5 nF -> 4.5 kHz audio low-pass.
* The 1 kohm / 10 nF input filters are 16 kHz anti-alias filters that keep
* the 1 MHz LO ripple out of the rectifier.
*
* Bias current sources are ideal for clarity; replace them with mirrors
* before layout.  rgval=1 on every analog MOS (rgval=0 gives a singular OP).
.subckt RX_AM_DEMOD i_in q_in out vdd vss
.param itail=500u rload=10k cload=3.5n

* ---- 1.55 V reference (matches the TIA output DC bias) -----------------
* A divider, not an RC average: the 1 ms verification transient is far
* shorter than the 10 ms time constant of a 16 Hz RC average.
Rref1 vdd bi 6.9k
Rref2 bi vss 3.1k
Rrefq1 vdd bq 6.9k
Rrefq2 bq vss 3.1k

* ---- 16 kHz anti-alias filters ----------------------------------------
Rfi i_in ii 1k
Cfi ii vss 10n
Rfq q_in qq 1k
Cfq qq vss 10n

* ---- I-channel half-wave rectifier ------------------------------------
X1 d1 ii tail vss NMOS_nf w=100u l=1u nf=4 rgval=1
X2 d2 bi tail vss NMOS_nf w=100u l=1u nf=4 rgval=1
Itail tail vss dc {itail}
* PMOS mirror: copy the input-branch current into the reference branch
X3 d1 d1 vdd vdd PMOS_nf w=50u l=2u nf=4 rgval=1
X4 d2 d1 vdd vdd PMOS_nf w=50u l=2u nf=4 rgval=1
* clamp the negative half, mirror the positive half to the output
X5 d2 d2 vss vss NMOS_nf w=100u l=1u nf=4 rgval=1
X6 out d2 vss vss NMOS_nf w=100u l=1u nf=4 rgval=1

* ---- Q-channel half-wave rectifier, summed at out ---------------------
X7 d3 qq tailq vss NMOS_nf w=100u l=1u nf=4 rgval=1
X8 d4 bq tailq vss NMOS_nf w=100u l=1u nf=4 rgval=1
Itailq tailq vss dc {itail}
X9 d3 d3 vdd vdd PMOS_nf w=50u l=2u nf=4 rgval=1
X10 d4 d3 vdd vdd PMOS_nf w=50u l=2u nf=4 rgval=1
X11 d4 d4 vss vss NMOS_nf w=100u l=1u nf=4 rgval=1
X12 out d4 vss vss NMOS_nf w=100u l=1u nf=4 rgval=1

* ---- shared output load / audio low-pass ------------------------------
Rload out vdd {rload}
Cload out vss {cload}
.ends RX_AM_DEMOD
